Description: Disable bytemuck nightly_portable_simd feature (incompatible with rustc-1.92.0)
 The bytemuck crate version 1.25.0 enables the nightly_portable_simd feature
 which adds Zeroable/Pod impls for core::simd::Simd<T, N>. This requires the
 portable_simd nightly feature via -Zallow-features=portable_simd. However,
 with rustc-1.92.0 (Debian system Rust), the stabilized portable_simd API
 requires an explicit "where LaneCount<N>: SupportedLaneCount" bound on
 generic impls, which bytemuck 1.25.0 does not supply. Removing this feature
 is safe because no Chromium code uses SIMD bytemuck traits in the CEF build.
Author: Juan Manuel Méndez Rey <juan.mendezr@proton.me>
Bug-Debian: https://bugs.debian.org/915400
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-04-07

